{"name":"Brooklyn","hex":"#586766","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Brooklyn","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nA borough in New York City, New York. It is located on the western end of Long Island. \n\nA town in Windham County, Connecticut. \nA village in St. Clair County, Illinois.\nA small town in Morgan County, Indiana.\nA small city in Poweshiek County, Iowa.\nA village in Jackson County, Michigan.\nA city in Cuyahoga County, Ohio, United States.\nA town in Green County, Wisconsin.\nA village in Dane County and Green County, Wisconsin.\nA town in Green Lake County, Wisconsin.\nA small town in Washburn County, Wisconsin.\nA number of townships in the United States, listed under Brooklyn Township.","A borough in New York City, New York. It is located on the western end of Long Island."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Brooklyn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brooklyn","blocks":[{"text":"Brooklyn, coextensive with Kings County, is the most populous of the five boroughs and counties of New York City, New York. Located at the westernmost end of Long Island and formerly an independent city, Brooklyn shares a land border with the borough and county of Queens. It has several bridge and tunnel connections to the borough of Manhattan, across the East River, including the architecturally significant Brooklyn Bridge, and is connected to Staten Island by the Verrazzano–Narrows Bridge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Brooklyn_skyline.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_skyline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brooklyn","wikidata":"Q18419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Prospect_Park_boathouse_%2861446p%29.jpg/500px-Prospect_Park_boathouse_%2861446p%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thum